      "writtenOn": "2024-08-15T22:42:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should preserve the behavior that `command-\u003emStatus` is updated regardless of `command-\u003emWaitStatus`. I see that whenever the code which creates a command sets `mWaitStatus`, it then uses the value of `mStatus` which is returned by `AudioCommandThread::sendCommand`. The weird thing is that if there is a non-zero delay, then `insertCommand_l` will reset `mWaitStatus`: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/av/services/audiopolicy/service/AudioPolicyService.cpp;l\u003d2674;drc\u003defb735f4d5a2f04550e33e8aa9485f906018fe4e. But the caller does not know about that and will still use `mStatus`! This logic is prone to surprises, for sure, so let\u0027s not disrupt it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2154,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 2154,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "ccb660dde2b12d3c7779167f50c3a0ebfd28bb38",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c83a25f_73a49623",
        "filename": "services/audiopolicy/service/AudioPolicyService.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 2154,
      "author": {
        "id": 3225096
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-16T17:37:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The main reason I did this change is because the race which might happen after the command is inserted to the queue by sendCommand()-\u003einsertCommand_l() and before sendCommand() returns (command-\u003emStatus). It looks that for \"non-waiting\" type of command (command-\u003emWaitStatus \u003d false (set after command created, before inserted to the queue)) following scenarios are possible:\n\n- sendCommand() returns NO_ERROR ( https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/av/services/audiopolicy/service/AudioPolicyService.h;l\u003d648 ) (when command thread is too slow to finish call to audioflinger before sendCommand() return, I assume most of the cases)\n- sendCommand() returns audioflinger call result (when command thread is fast enough to finish audioflinger call before sendCommand() return)\n\nNow with proposed change (command-\u003emStatus \u003d status set only for \"waiting\" commands under command-\u003emLock) it is at least secured that for \"non-waiting\" commands sendCommand() returned status will be always NO_ERROR and for \"waiting\" commands the status will be audioflinger call result (or TIMED_OUT in case hang happens).",
      "parentUuid": "faec9d60_22093335",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2154,
        "startChar": 24,
